3.2. Signal preprocessing
The raw motion data collected from smartwatch sensors were processed before feature extraction and model development. For the two-stage deep learning pipeline, signals were segmented into fixed-length windows of 2048 time steps across six sensor channels, representing three accelerometer axes and three gyroscope axes. For the handcrafted feature pipeline, each recording was segmented independently into 512-sample windows with a step size of 128 samples, corresponding to 75% overlap. This produced 74,102 segments, or approximately 158 segments per patient on average. Independent segmentation ensured that no segment crossed recording or task boundaries.
