3.8. Classification scenarios
Four classification scenarios were defined. The first used only demographic and questionnaire variables in a three-class setting. The second addressed a binary PD-versus-non-PD problem. The third distinguished PD from other movement disorders. The fourth applied the full two-stage framework to three-class classification using learned embeddings.
The unified three-class experiment constituted the primary evaluation of the proposed framework. The binary scenarios were included as auxiliary diagnostic analyses to isolate specific class boundaries, quantify pairwise separability, and help explain the failure modes observed in the three-class setting. They were not used to support the main comparative claim and were not presented as alternatives to the unified three-class task.
