5.8.2. Inter-class separability and directional confusion
Pairwise ROC-AUC analysis showed that the difficulty of the three-class task was not distributed uniformly across class boundaries. For the handcrafted ensemble, Healthy–PD and Healthy–Other Movement Disorders achieved AUC values of 0.931 and 0.903, respectively, whereas PD–Other Movement Disorders achieved the lowest AUC of 0.773. The same pattern was more pronounced in the deep pipeline, where PD–Other Movement Disorders achieved an AUC of 0.711. These findings quantitatively confirm that the principal source of three-class difficulty is the boundary between the two symptomatic diagnostic groups (see Table 14).
