5.8.4. Out-of-fold SHAP explainability analysis
The out-of-fold SHAP analysis showed that the XGBoost component relied on a combination of wavelet, frequency-domain, tremor-power, and time-domain variability descriptors rather than on a single dominant variable. The highest global patient-level SHAP importance was observed for wavelet_11, with a mean absolute SHAP value of 0.0786. This was followed by fd_ch3_tremor_pwr at 0.0736, fd_ch1_tremor_pwr at 0.0600, fd_ch2_b1 at 0.0584, and fd_ch0_b1 at 0.0550.
Other highly ranked variables included wavelet_5 (0.0537), fd_ch1_b2 (0.0530), fd_ch4_b0 (0.0524), fd_ch5_b1 (0.0481), and fd_ch3_b2 (0.0468). These findings indicate that the classifier relied on a distributed combination of multi-scale waveform structure, tremor-band power, broader spectral-band characteristics, and time-domain variability. This finding is consistent with the handcrafted feature-group ablation, in which removing the frequency-domain group produced the largest reduction in patient-level accuracy. The global importance ranking is shown in Fig. 3.
Class-specific attribution patterns differed across the three outputs. Healthy-control predictions were most strongly influenced by wavelet_11, fd_ch4_b0, wavelet_5, fd_ch1_b2, and fd_ch3_tremor_pwr. Parkinson’s disease predictions were influenced primarily by frequency-band descriptors, including fd_ch2_b1, fd_ch0_b1, fd_ch3_b2, fd_ch3_b0, and fd_ch5_b2. Other Movement Disorders predictions were most strongly influenced by fd_ch3_tremor_pwr, fd_ch1_tremor_pwr, fd_ch5_b1, td_ch4_iqr, and td_ch2_iqr. The class-specific attribution patterns are shown in Fig. 4.
The shared contribution of frequency-band and tremor-power descriptors to Parkinson’s disease and Other Movement Disorders outputs provides a feature-level explanation for the reduced separability between these symptomatic groups. These SHAP values should be interpreted as model-specific predictive attributions rather than causal clinical biomarkers.
Full per-class SHAP summary plots, showing the distribution of feature values and their signed contributions across all out-of-fold segments, are provided for each class in Supplementary Figures S1–S3.
